    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "These types are inferred as `any`. A way to get it typed correctly would be like so:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n// ...\r\n\r\nconst { indexName = null } = props || ({} as IndexProps);\r\n\r\nif (indexName === null) {\r\n  throw new Error(withUsage('The `indexName` option is required.'));\r\n}\r\n\r\n// At this point, `indexId` and `indexName` are strings\r\nconst { indexId = indexName } = props || ({} as IndexProps);\r\n```",
    "commit_id": "8eb6bb1911050aa07cdcb578471e024a4830e3a1",
    "created_at": "2019-08-26T12:27:42Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -106,7 +107,7 @@ function resolveScopedResultsFromIndex(widget: Index): ScopedResult[] {\n }\n \n const index = (props: IndexProps): Index => {\n-  const { indexName = null } = props || {};\n+  const { indexName = null, indexId = indexName } = props || {};",
