    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The switch to optional is not required we lose the type-safety. An alternative is to check the value even though the compiler ensure the value is always available. At least TypeScript users (mainly us) don't lose type-safety.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst index = (props: IndexProps): Index => {\r\n  if (!props) {\r\n    throw new Error(withUsage('Cannot be called without args.'));\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const { indexName = null, indexId = indexName } = props;\r\n\r\n  if (indexName === null) {\r\n    throw new Error(withUsage('The `indexName` option is required.'));\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (indexId === null) {\r\n    // Should not happen but at least the compiler is happy.\r\n    throw new Error(withUsage(\"The `indexId` option can't be `null`.\"));\r\n  }\r\n   \r\n  // ...\r\n```",
    "commit_id": "8eb6bb1911050aa07cdcb578471e024a4830e3a1",
    "created_at": "2019-08-27T10:38:18Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -105,8 +106,12 @@ function resolveScopedResultsFromIndex(widget: Index): ScopedResult[] {\n   return resolveScopedResultsFromWidgets(widgetSiblings);\n }\n \n-const index = (props: IndexProps): Index => {\n-  const { indexName = null } = props || {};\n+const index = (props?: IndexProps): Index => {",
